  "title": "Kourovka problem 20.67 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Suppose that G is a finite group, p is a prime, and B is a Brauer p-block of\nG with defect group D. Let cd(B) be the set of degrees of the irreducible complex\ncharacters in B.\n   a) Is it true that the derived length of D is bounded by |cd(B)|?\n   b) (A. Jaikin-Zapirain). Is is even true that |cd(D)| ⩽ |cd(B)|?     G. Navarro",
